__init__ is the method Python uses to initialize an object when it is created. It sets up the object’s initial data, like name, age, or balance.

Simple meaning
When you create an object from a class, Python calls __init__ automatically.

python
class Student:
    def __init__(self, name, age):
        self.name = name
        self.age = age

s1 = Student("Asha", 21)
Here:

Student is the class.

s1 is the object.

__init__ stores "Asha" and 21 inside that object.

Why it is useful
Without __init__, you would have to set values manually after creating the object. __init__ helps create the object in a ready-to-use state.

Easy example
python
class Car:
    def __init__(self, brand, color):
        self.brand = brand
        self.color = color

car1 = Car("Toyota", "Red")
print(car1.brand)
print(car1.color)
This means:

brand becomes "Toyota"

color becomes "Red"

Important points
self refers to the current object.

__init__ runs automatically.

It does not create the object; it only initializes it.

It usually does not return anything.

Interview answer
You can say:

“__init__ is a special method in Python that initializes an object’s attributes when the object is created. It is called automatically and helps set the object’s initial state.”

If you want, I can also explain self in the same simple way.

can you given an example without __init__
Yes — you can create a class without __init__, but then the object starts out empty and you set attributes later.

Example without __init__
python
class Student:
    pass

s1 = Student()
s1.name = "Asha"
s1.age = 21

print(s1.name)
print(s1.age)
What is happening
Student() creates an object.

pass means the class has no methods or logic yet.

name and age are added after the object is created.

Compare with __init__
With __init__, you set values while creating the object:

python
class Student:
    def __init__(self, name, age):
        self.name = name
        self.age = age

s1 = Student("Asha", 21)
Difference
Without __init__: attributes are added manually after object creation.

With __init__: attributes are initialized automatically when the object is created.

Interview answer
You can say:

“Yes, a class can be created without __init__. In that case, the object is created first and its attributes are assigned later manually. __init__ is useful because it initializes the object at the time of creation.”